lesson k-plan-the-path v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=5 subject=coding levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Plan the path"
  goal "Plan the steps that take a robot to the flag before it moves."

  look {
    scene 12x10 {
      maze g cols=4 rows=3 col=1 row=1 flag=[3, 2] trail=none at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
        Before the robot moves, we plan: two steps right, then one step down. A good plan reaches the
        flag. If a rock is in the way, we plan a way round it.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.which-program k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.which-program count=2 seed=2 hard-count=3
    practice k.steps-to-goal count=3 seed=3 easy-count=1 hard-count=2
    show k.go-round-rock k=0 hard-k=1
    show k.guide-the-teddy
    practice k.rabbit-hops count=1 seed=9 easy-count=0
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.two-ways-work
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.plan-past-rocks
  }
  remember {
    say "Plan the steps first, then let the robot go."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question and each plan aloud. Follow the arrows traced a program someone else wrote;
    this lesson is the step on from it, the child making the plan. The teddy game is for you to
    watch: the child should say the plan before moving the teddy. If the child is stuck, walk the
    path on floor tiles first. Off the page, plan a route through the house to a hidden toy. Japan,
    幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten guidelines), 環境, 内容 (7):
    "身近な物や遊具に興味をもってかかわり，考えたり，試したりして工夫して遊ぶ。" (Take an interest in familiar
    things and toys, and play inventively by thinking and trying things out.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level a plan of three right and one down is chosen in the teacher's pen first, the flag is far to the right, and the rock sits next to the robot."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the flag is close, the plans are easy to swap, and the rock sits further along the row."
  }
}
